---
import { u } from '../lib/url';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  section="Page"
  title="AI"
  kicker="Disclosure"
  description="How generative AI is used to build this site, and which content is written by hand."
  wide={false}
>
  <div class="prose-nw">
    <p>
      This page follows the <a href="https://www.bydamo.la/p/ai-manifesto">/ai manifesto</a>: a
      plain statement of where generative AI is used, so you can decide how much to trust what you
      read.
    </p>

    <h2>The site is built with AI</h2>
    <p>
      Most of this site was made by AI. I use <a href="https://claude.ai/code">Claude Code</a>{' '}
      (Anthropic's Claude models) to write and maintain the code: the Astro pages, layouts,
      components, Tailwind styles, build scripts, GitHub Actions workflows, the SEO audit, and the
      style guide. I describe what I want, review the pull requests, and merge them. The repository
      is public on <a href="https://github.com/noahweidig/noahweidig.github.io">GitHub</a>, and the
      commit history shows which changes came from AI sessions.
    </p>

    <h2>The writing is mine</h2>
    <p>
      I write my blog posts, publication abstracts, and the descriptions of my research, awards, and
      experience myself. AI does not draft them, and I don't publish AI-generated text as my own
      thinking.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the line gets blurry</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Site copy such as page intros, meta descriptions, and UI labels may be drafted or edited by
        AI, and I review it.
      </li>
      <li>
        Generated images, such as social cards and blog covers, come from scripts in the repository.
      </li>
      <li>
        Content that is only formatted, structured, or checked by AI (typo fixes, frontmatter,
        links) is still my writing.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Accountability</h2>
    <p>
      I review what ships, and mistakes are mine. If you spot an error,{' '}
      <a href={u('/contact/')}>tell me</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
